# Rocci in five minutes

You will type a tiny greeting component, preview it, and see
**Hello, Ada** in the window. Inspecting the generated Roc comes after
that.

Until an installed `rocci` exists, prefix each `rocci` command with
`cargo run -q -p rocci-cli --` from the repository root.

## Type a greeting

From the clone, create `Hello.rocci` with this complete module:

```rocci
import Html

@component
Hello = |{ name }|
    <p>Hello, <strong>{name}</strong></p>
```

Preview it:

```sh
rocci view Hello.rocci --component Hello --arg name=Ada
```

Rocci compiles the module, starts a local HTTP server, prints the URL,
and opens the native preview window. Add `--no-window` and open the URL
yourself if you do not want the webview.

The greeting should read **Hello, Ada**.

A larger cataloged file with scoped CSS lives at
[Styling.rocci](/examples/styling/source/Styling-rocci/).

## If it failed

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `roc` not found | Toolchain | [Install](/docs/install/) |
| Unknown component | Name mismatch | Use `Hello` or `hello` |
| No window | Webview / display | Rerun with `--no-window` and open the printed URL |

## Inspect the generated Roc

This heading is optional. Lower the file you typed:

```sh
rocci build Hello.rocci
```

Stdout is ordinary Roc. Find `hello = |{ name }|`. The PascalCase
component `Hello` became a camelCase function. Rocci did not type-check
the module; Roc will, when you run or view it.

| Authored | Generated |
| --- | --- |
| `@component Hello = \|{ name }\|` | `hello : { name : Str } -> Html` and `hello = \|{ name }\|` |
| `<p>Hello, <strong>{name}</strong></p>` | `Html.element` calls; `{name}` becomes `Html.text(name)` and must be `Str` |

Next: [Components](/docs/templates/components/).
